Z||000000||Dan87GT||11-15-2000||08:37 AM||||Has anybody ever installed a retractable antenna on their car, I thought maybe with a little metal trimming it might be possible. Any thoughts????? This would be a replacement for the stock location||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-15-2000||11:54 AM||||i haven't done it.. i just fiber-glased over where mine was. but there is PLENTY of room under there and don't see why there would be any problem fitting it there. you just have to run power and acc. lead from the radio for it's activation. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||the need for speed||11-15-2000||03:48 PM||||i have always like the 300zx retractable antenna!could look good on the fiero in the same location as the fuel cap but on the other side.Does any one have any pics of the 300zx antenna out there||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||11-15-2000||04:49 PM||||I hope I'm not doing anything wrong here, but I found a picture on eBay.  You can find it at:  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499339551" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499339551</A>   Nice car.  I'm getting one next.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-15-2000||04:56 PM||||It can be done in the stock location. I looked under there once to check for clearance. You need about 11"-14" to do it. I am planning on doing it during my rebuild. I never use the radio anyway.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||the need for speed||11-15-2000||05:41 PM||||can any one get a closer shot of the 300zx  antenna. i like how it angles back a little!does any one now if there is enough space in the back of the fiero???<P>are 300z front wheel drive or rear????||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||11-15-2000||06:44 PM||||I couldn't find a closer shot, but I found one with the antenna down.  It's at:  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499369927" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499369927</A>   Don't know if they're front or back wheel; I'd guess back wheel?<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||11-16-2000||03:20 AM||||300ZX's are rear wheel drive||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||11-16-2000||09:21 PM||||I found a non powered (i.e. not retractable) antenna at Walmarts last week that would work great.  It's only about an inch and a half high.  It has some sort of booster connected to it.  Seems like it would be a good compromise between the cost and installation difficulties of a power antenna and the looks of a stock unit.  It was only about $15.  It might not be good for really long distances, but unless you're planning on traveling, I don't see why it would matter much.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||11-16-2000||09:43 PM||||I found a little better picture of the antenna when it's down.  I think it would look good with that little antenna!  Anyway, it's at:  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499316181" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=499316181</A>   Nice car!!!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
